# Cloudflare Tunnel — Configuration
#
# This file documents the tunnel configuration used by cloudflared.
# The actual token-based authentication is passed via the
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN environment variable in docker-compose.yml.
#
# For manual setup (non-Docker), create a tunnel with:
#   cloudflared tunnel create photo-portfolio
#   cloudflared tunnel route dns photo-portfolio photo.patriciobet.dev
#   cloudflared tunnel route dns photo-portfolio admin-photo.patriciobet.dev
#
# Then configure routes in ~/.cloudflared/config.yml or via the dashboard.

# ── Tunnel Routes ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tunnel routes are configured in the Cloudflare dashboard or via CLI:
#
# Route 1: photo.patriciobet.dev → Caddy (:8080)
# Route 2: admin-photo.patriciobet.dev → Caddy (:8080)
# Route 3: cdn-photo.patriciobet.dev → R2 public bucket (direct, no tunnel)
#
# DNS records in Cloudflare:
#   photo.patriciobet.dev    CNAME  <tunnel-uuid>.cfargotunnel.com
#   admin-photo.patriciobet.dev CNAME <tunnel-uuid>.cfargotunnel.com
#   cdn-photo.patriciobet.dev  CNAME  <r2-public-bucket>.<account-id>.r2.cloudflareresource.com
#
# ── Health Check ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflared reports health via the /ready endpoint.
# docker-compose.yml uses the token-based run command which
# includes automatic health monitoring and auto-restart.
#
# ── Auto-restart ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker restart policy: unless-stopped
# Cloudflared internal: --no-autoupdate prevents unexpected version changes
#
# ── Troubleshooting ───────────────────────────────────────────
# View tunnel status: cloudflared tunnel info <tunnel-name>
# View tunnel logs:   cloudflared tunnel logs <tunnel-name>
# List routes:        cloudflared tunnel list-routes <tunnel-name>
# Delete tunnel:      cloudflared tunnel cleanup <tunnel-name>
